[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($tmp, 'The tattoo: Large asymmetric crescent composition. Sensual body flow. sophisticated contemporary Neo-Tribal tattoo design built from bold saturated black forms, sweeping organic curves, sharp tapered hooks, controlled points, dramatic thick-to-thin transitions and intentional untouched negative space; treat black and exposed skin as equally important parts of the composition; design specifically for the stated body location so the artwork follows anatomy, musculature, joints and natural directional flow rather than appearing like a centered graphic pasted onto the body; freely vary between organic flowing forms, sculptural abstraction, armor-like structures, exoskeletal and biomechanical influence, creature abstraction, Y2K Neo-Tribal revival, minimal compositions, fragmented forms, heavy blackwork, elegant negative-space compositions and experimental contemporary Neo-Tribal according to the individual concept; some pieces may be symmetrical, others radically asymmetric; some may contain huge saturated-black fields while others may use only a few restrained black forms; vary density, scale, rhythm and visual weight aggressively across the collection; preserve clean tattooable edges and intentional skin breaks; when a creature or recognizable source inspires the concept, REDUCE the subject into Neo-Tribal form rather than drawing a normal illustrative animal and surrounding it with tribal decoration; contemporary abstract Neo-Tribal only, do not imitate or fabricate Polynesian, Maori, Samoan, Bornean or other culturally specific traditional tattoo patterns, and do not invent cultural meanings; avoid generic 1990s tribal clip art, centered logo-like emblems, repetitive flame shapes, generic symmetrical tribal stamps and thin thorny cybersigilism; this is Neo-Tribal, not Cybersigilism, prioritize bold sculptural black mass, physical movement, negative space and anatomical flow over delicate technological sigils; black ink is dominant, with very rare selective dark-red accent only when the individual concept explicitly requests it; no lettering, no words, no watermark; the finished result must look like exceptional contemporary tattoo work that a serious Neo-Tribal artist could actually execute. In the right panel it is on a woman, hip to thigh, wearing low-rise black shorts and a simple black crop top', (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding $false))
